## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement policy-based gating and cross-account state references in production workflows.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform Cloud and Sentinel policy gating
- remote_state across AWS accounts
- per-environment workspaces (qa/prod)
- CI integration for plan upload and gate checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Sentinel-like policy (illustrative)
import "tfplan/v2"
import "strings"

let prodChange = false
for (rc in tfplan.resource_changes) {
  if (strings.contains(rc.address, ".prod.")) {
    if (rc.change.actions.includes("create") || rc.change.actions.includes("update") || rc.change.actions.includes("delete")) {
      prodChange = true
    }
  }
}
function main() { return !prodChange }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle multi-resource prod groups with blue/green deployments?
- What failure modes exist if remote_state is unavailable during plan?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests multi-account Terraform patterns: provider aliases, cross-account data sources, and deterministic apply order.

## Key Concepts

- Aliased providers
- Cross-account data sources
- Data referencing across providers
- depends_on for ordering
- Credentials management via profiles and assume_role

## Code Example

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "prod"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "prod"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "audit"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "audit"
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "prod" {
  provider = aws.prod
}

data "aws_s3_bucket" "prod_bucket" {
  provider = aws.prod
  bucket   = "my-prod-bucket"
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "audit" {
  provider = aws.audit
  statement {
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject"]
    resources = ["${data.aws_s3_bucket.prod_bucket.arn}/*"]
    principals {
      type        = "AWS"
      identifiers = ["arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.prod.account_id}:root"]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "audit_bucket" {
  provider = aws.audit
  bucket   = "audit-bucket"
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "audit_policy" {
  provider = aws.audit
  name     = "CrossAccountGetObject"
  policy   = data.aws_iam_policy_document.audit.json
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate credentials for the aliased providers safely?
- How would you test this cross-account permission in a CI workflow?
